{title: A Seat of Honor}
{subtitle: 2 Kings 25:27; Jeremiah 52:31; 2 Kings 25:28; Jeremiah 52:32; 2 Kings 25:29; Jeremiah 52:33}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Dm] | [Eb] | [Bb] [Dm] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]The thir-ty-sev-enth year of exile [Gm7]passed
[Eb]In the twelfth month when hope ar[Bb]rived [F/A]
[Gm]E-vil-Me-ro-dach became [Dm]king of Babylon
[Eb]And the heavy chains were [Fsus4]lifted [F]high
[Eb]He showed favor to the cap[Gm]tive king
[Eb]Who sat in darkness for so [Fsus4]long
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]He spoke [Bb]kindly to [Dm]him with [Eb]grace
[Bb/D]Gave a [Cm7]seat of honor [Dm]in that [Eb]place
Above [Gm]the thrones of oth[Bbmaj7/F]er kings
Jehoiac[Eb]hin heard the sweet [Bb]things
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The prison clothes were [F/A]taken a[Gm]way [Bbmaj7/F]
[Eb]Restored to his dignity that [Bb]day [F/A]
[Gm]He ate regularly at the [Dm7]royal table
[Eb]For the rest of his [F]life
The [Eb]daily allowance was provid[Gm]ed [Gm7/F]
[Eb]In the land where he was [F]exiled
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
He spoke [Bb]kindly to [Dm]him with [Eb]grace
[Bb/D]Gave a [Cm7]seat of honor [Dm]in that [Eb]place
Above [Gm]the thrones of oth[F6]er kings
Jehoiac[Eb]hin heard the sweet [Bb]things
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]From the shadows of the [Gm]cell
To the light where the honor [Eb]dwell
A glimmer of hope re[Gm]mains
In the memories of old [Eb]days
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Released from [Bb]prison in the [Eb]end
With [Cm7]kindness that we [F7]cannot mend [Bb][Bbmaj7/D][Eb][Bb]
{end_of_verse}
